"surface":"எழிற்கலை","parts":[{"text":"எழில்","lemma":"எழில்","gloss":"beautiful"},{"text":"கலை","lemma":"கலை","gloss":"male stag"}],"gloss":"beautiful stag"},{"surface":"புலிப்பால்","parts":[{"text":"புலி","lemma":"புலி","gloss":"tiger"},{"text":"பால்","lemma":"பால்","gloss":"side/clutches"}],"gloss":"to the tiger's clutches"},{"surface":"பட்டெனச்","parts":[{"text":"பட்டெனச்","lemma":"பட்டெனச்","gloss":"because it fell"}],"gloss":"because it fell","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சிறுமறி","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறுமை","gloss":"small"},{"text":"மறி","lemma":"மறி","gloss":"fawn"}],"gloss":"small fawn"},{"surface":"தழீஇய","parts":[{"text":"தழீஇய","lemma":"தழுவு","gloss":"having embraced"}],"gloss":"embracing"},{"surface":"தெறிநடை","parts":[{"text":"தெறி","lemma":"தெறி","gloss":"skipping"},{"text":"நடை","lemma":"நடை","gloss":"gait"}],"gloss":"skipping gait"},{"surface":"மடப்பிணை","parts":[{"text":"மட","lemma":"மடமை","gloss":"gentle"},{"text":"பிணை","lemma":"பிணை","gloss":"female deer"}],"gloss":"gentle doe"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூளை","parts":[{"text":"பூளை","lemma":"பூளை","gloss":"Pūḷai plant"}],"gloss":"Pūḷai plant"},{"surface":"நீடிய","parts":[{"text":"நீடிய","lemma":"நீடு","gloss":"grown tall"}],"gloss":"grown tall"},{"surface":"வெருவரு","parts":[{"text":"வெரு","lemma":"வெரு","gloss":"fear"},{"text":"வரு","lemma":"வரு","gloss":"causing"}],"gloss":"fear-inducing"},{"surface":"பறந்தலை","parts":[{"text":"பறந்தலை","lemma":"பறந்தலை","gloss":"wasteland"}],"gloss":"wasteland"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேளை","parts":[{"text":"வேளை","lemma":"வேளை","gloss":"Vēḷai plant"}],"gloss":"Vēḷai plant"},{"surface":"வெண்பூக்","parts":[{"text":"வெண்பூக்","lemma":"வெண்பூக்","gloss":"white flower"}],"gloss":"white flower","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கறிக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கறிக்கும்","lemma":"கறி","gloss":"grazes on"}],"gloss":"grazes on"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆளில்","parts":[{"text":"ஆள்","lemma":"ஆள்","gloss":"person"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"devoid of people"},{"surface":"அத்தம்","parts":[{"text":"அத்தம்","lemma":"அத்தம்","gloss":"wasteland"}],"gloss":"wasteland"},{"surface":"ஆகிய","parts":[{"text":"ஆகிய","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"which became"}],"gloss":"which became"},{"surface":"காடே","parts":[{"text":"காடு","lemma":"காடு","gloss":"forest"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"the forest indeed"}]}],"literal":"Having grown weary of the elephant-post stations with blemish-free, strong-cored wood, / and the water ghats muddied because male elephants bathed and drank there, / wearing a garland of green leaves of the dark, fragrant Kadamba tree, / like the retinue of Murugan who causes fear and affliction, your / fierce warriors with curved bows and sharp, good arrows, / taking what they wanted, and leaving behind the unwanted remnants, / and the fields scattered with usable goods left behind, / because sharp axes struck in every village, / the groves where tutelary trees were shaken, and the tall mansions / of artistically crafted good houses, destroyed by hot fire, / looking at the regions where roaring fire raged, / marching against daily so that enemies feel ashamed, / \"He will do still more such things; no one / can approach him, such is his resolve,\" they say, / as the vast army gathered, making the earth groan, / you who won the battle at Alanganam and destroyed [them], / O one with the strength of Death! Having seen you, I return. / Because a beautiful stag with branched horns fell to a tiger, / the gentle doe with a skipping gait, embracing her small fawn, / in the fear-inducing wasteland where Pūḷai plants grow tall, / grazes on the white flowers of the Vēḷai plant, / in the forest that has become a wasteland devoid of people.","translation":"Having grown weary of the elephant-post stations made of strong, blemish-free wood, and the water ghats muddied by bathing and drinking elephants; wearing garlands of green leaves from the dark, fragrant Kadamba tree, like the terrifying retinue of Lord Murugan, your fierce warriors with curved bows and sharp arrows plundered what they wanted and left the rest to waste, scattering the fields. In every village, tutelary trees were felled by sharp axes, and artistically crafted mansions were consumed by raging fires. Looking upon these ruined regions, your enemies are filled with shame as you march against them daily. People say, 'He will do still more; his resolve is such that none can approach him.' With a vast army that made the earth groan, you won the great battle of Alanganam and destroyed your foes, O king with the strength of Death! Having seen you, I now return. In the enemy's land, because the beautiful stag with branched horns fell prey to a tiger, the gentle doe with a skipping gait embraces her little fawn and grazes on the white flowers of the Vēḷai plant, in the fear-inducing wasteland overgrown with tall Pūḷai weeds—a forest now utterly devoid of people.","modern":"குற்றமற்ற வலிமையான தூண்களைக் கொண்ட யானை கட்டும் கம்பங்களை வெறுத்து, களிறுகள் மூழ்கி நீர் குடித்ததால் கலங்கிய நீர்நிலைகளையும்; கார் காலத்து நறிய கடம்ப மரத்தின் பசிய இலைகளாலாகிய மாலையை அணிந்து, அச்சம் தரும் முருகனின் பூதப்படை போன்ற உன்னுடைய கூர்மையான அம்புகளையும் வளைந்த வில்லையும் உடைய வீரர்கள் கொள்ளையடிக்க வேண்டியவற்றைக் கொண்டு, வேண்டாதவற்றை வீசி எறிந்த வயல்களையும்; கூர்மையான கோடரிகள் பாய்ந்ததால் ஒவ்வொரு ஊரிலும் காவல் மரங்கள் சாய்ந்த சோலைகளையும்; அழகிய வேலைப்பாடுகள் அமைந்த நல்ல வீடுகளைக் கொடிய நெருப்பு அழித்ததால், பெருநெருப்பு எரிந்து தணிந்த இடங்களையும் பார்த்து; பகைவர்கள் நாணமடையும்படி நாள்தோறும் படையெடுத்துச் சென்று, 'இவன் இன்னும் பலவற்றைச் செய்வான்; இவனை நெருங்குவது எவருக்கும் இயலாது' என்று கூறும் துணிவுடையவன் நீ. நிலம் நெளியும்படி திரண்ட பெரிய படையுடன் ஆலங்கானத்துப் போரில் பகைவர்களை வென்று அழித்த கூற்றுவனைப் போன்ற வலிமையுடையவனே! உன்னைக் கண்டு நான் வருகின்றேன். கிளைத்த கொம்புகளையுடைய அழகிய ஆண் மான் புலியின் வாயில் பட்டதால், குதித்து நடக்கும் மென்மையான பெண் மான் தன் குட்டியைத் தழுவிக்கொண்டு, பூளைச் செடிகள் வளர்ந்து அச்சம் தரும் பாழ்வெளியில், வேளைச் செடியின் வெண்மையான பூக்களை மேய்கிறது. அது மனிதர்களே இல்லாத காடாக மாறிவிட்டது.","explanation":"The poet Kallāṭaṉār addresses the Pāṇḍiyaṉ king Talaiyālaṅkāṉattu Neṭuñceḻiyaṉ in this poem of the vākai (victory) tiṇai. He praises the king's absolute victory at the battle of Alanganam, describing the complete devastation of the enemy's territory. The poet contrasts the king's terrifying military might with the desolate landscape of the conquered territory. The image of the gentle doe grazing on wild weeds (vēḷai, pūḷai) in a deserted wasteland because her mate was killed by a tiger mirrors the plight of the enemy's subjects and wives whose protectors were slain by the king (the tiger). Key words include ālaṅkāṉam (the battlefield), kālam (Death/Yama), and attam (deserted wasteland).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.17],[1.17,1.6],[1.6,2.03],[2.03,3.2],[3.2,3.6],[3.6,4.24],[4.24,4.76],[4.76,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,6.46],[6.46,6.8],[6.8,7.55],[7.55,8.3],[8.3,8.6],[8.6,8.9],[8.9,9.3],[9.3,9.75],[9.75,10.2],[10.2,10.9],[10.9,11.45],[11.45,12.0],[12.0,12.2],[12.2,12.62],[12.62,13.19],[13.19,13.9],[13.9,14.3],[14.3,14.5],[14.5,14.9],[14.9,15.58],[15.58,16.12],[16.12,16.8],[16.8,17.4],[18.68,19.28],[19.28,19.48],[19.48,19.98],[19.98,20.38],[20.38,21.78],[21.78,21.98],[21.98,22.43],[22.43,22.93],[22.93,23.38],[23.38,23.82],[23.82,24.38],[24.38,24.89],[24.89,25.58],[25.58,25.88],[25.88,26.18],[26.18,26.58],[26.58,27.98],[27.98,28.48],[28.48,28.98],[28.98,29.43],[29.43,29.88],[29.88,30.25],[30.25,30.88],[30.88,31.18],[31.18,31.73],[31.73,32.28],[32.28,32.58],[32.58,33.38],[33.38,33.63],[33.63,34.08],[34.08,34.88],[34.88,35.18],[35.96,36.46],[36.46,36.66],[36.66,37.06],[37.06,37.36],[37.36,37.56],[37.56,38.96],[38.96,39.34],[39.47,39.72],[39.72,40.55],[40.55,41.31],[41.31,41.5],[41.5,42.56],[42.56,42.96],[42.96,43.56],[43.56,44.06],[44.06,44.46],[44.46,45.39],[45.39,45.76],[45.76,46.12],[46.17,46.